@title Place macro from a generated page: it lands on the first drawing page, not on the contents table
@area Schematic
@sizes 1366x768
# Open the generated Table of contents (page 0a) and place a macro from Ctrl+K "Place macro". The macro used to be drawn on top of the table; now the canvas goes to page 1 and the macro is placed there. The pictures are the evidence.
click_text "Open example"
wait 40
click_text Pages
wait 20
# The page rows are painted, not labelled: the row "0a Table of contents" of the Pages panel.
click 142 313
wait 30
shot 01-contents-page-open
key ctrl+k
wait 6
text place macro
wait 8
key Enter
wait 20
shot 02-place-macro-window
click_text "Heater with thermostat"
wait 15
shot 03-macro-picked
click 66 417
wait 30
expect "Placed Heater with thermostat"
shot 04-placed-on-page-1
check_layout
